1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,500
Little Moments.

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,333
The Red Sock Mystery.

3
00:00:03,333 --> 00:00:07,240
Saturday morning, Mom drops a basket of clean laundry on the couch.

4
00:00:07,240 --> 00:00:10,927
It's warm, fluffy, and much taller than it looked in the dryer.

5
00:00:10,927 --> 00:00:13,156
Can you help me fold these, Ben?

6
00:00:13,420 --> 00:00:15,893
Only if I can be in charge of socks.

7
00:00:15,893 --> 00:00:17,882
I'm very good at socks.

8
00:00:18,172 --> 00:00:21,853
Five minutes later, he hands me a red sock and a striped sock.

9
00:00:21,853 --> 00:00:23,645
These two don't match.

10
00:00:23,932 --> 00:00:25,780
They both fit on feet.

11
00:00:25,780 --> 00:00:27,197
That's something.

12
00:00:27,484 --> 00:00:29,790
There should be another red one somewhere.

13
00:00:29,790 --> 00:00:33,009
Check the bigger clothes before we blame the washing machine.

14
00:00:33,292 --> 00:00:35,004
We shake out a towel.

15
00:00:35,004 --> 00:00:36,202
Nothing.

16
00:00:36,202 --> 00:00:38,015
We check a pillowcase.

17
00:00:38,015 --> 00:00:39,536
Still nothing.

18
00:00:39,536 --> 00:00:42,484
Ben holds up Dad's sweatshirt and makes it dance.

19
00:00:42,748 --> 00:00:44,710
Maybe the sock moved away.

20
00:00:44,710 --> 00:00:46,877
Maybe it wanted a bigger closet.

21
00:00:47,164 --> 00:00:48,251
Wait.

22
00:00:48,251 --> 00:00:50,356
There's a little lump in that sleeve.

23
00:00:50,356 --> 00:00:52,022
Turn it inside out.

24
00:00:52,300 --> 00:00:53,377
Aha!

25
00:00:53,377 --> 00:00:56,773
One red sock, hiding from its responsibilities.

26
00:00:57,052 --> 00:00:59,598
We put the pair together and finish the basket.

27
00:00:59,598 --> 00:01:02,744
I fold shirts while Ben matches the rest of the socks.

28
00:01:02,744 --> 00:01:05,702
This time, he checks the colors and patterns.

29
00:01:05,980 --> 00:01:07,359
Nice work.

30
00:01:07,359 --> 00:01:09,234
You two make a good team.

31
00:01:09,508 --> 00:01:11,739
Do good teams get a snack break?

32
00:01:11,980 --> 00:01:13,922
Mom points toward the kitchen.

33
00:01:13,922 --> 00:01:17,588
Ben races off, then comes back holding one striped sock.

34
00:01:17,860 --> 00:01:19,385
Small problem.

35
00:01:19,385 --> 00:01:21,291
This one is alone now.

36
00:01:21,580 --> 00:01:23,470
I look at the empty basket.

37
00:01:23,470 --> 00:01:25,376
The mystery is not over.

38
00:01:25,376 --> 00:01:29,167
Our snack break, however, is absolutely still happening.
